2. Permission for academic reproduction

Subject to these terms, permission is granted, without a fee or an individual
application, to download, make working copies of, inspect, run and modify the
Materials solely for academic reproduction.

"Academic reproduction" means non-commercial scholarly work directed at
reproducing, checking or independently validating the methods and numerical
findings supported by this package. It includes adapting code to a computing
environment, adjusting parameters, retraining models, rerunning simulations,
recomputing statistics and regenerating plots to carry out that verification.

You may report your verification methods and findings in academic reports or
publications, with attribution under section 3. This permission does not
authorize redistribution of the original or modified Materials.

